# gvisor.env — the ONE place the gVisor release is pinned (setec#89).
#
# The installer image ships no gVisor (owner decision D70, 2026-10-05). A node
# that runs the gvisor backend gets runsc from its own node preparation: the
# staging cloud-init, the EKS node-prep, or an administrator.
#
# Consumers of this pin carry no version of their own:
#   .github/workflows/e2e.yml       lays gVisor on the kind test node, as node
#                                   preparation does on a real node
#   development/k3s/scripts/*       source it when preparing a node by hand
# scripts/check-runtime-pins.sh fails CI when a consumer re-adds a literal, or
# when Dockerfile.installer names gVisor again.
#
# Lay THE WHOLE TARBALL, NOT A PRUNE. Measured on release-20260928.0: with only
# runsc and containerd-shim-runsc-v1 on disk, runsc dies at sandbox creation
# with `sidecar "gvisor_sentry" not usable ... --sidecar-usage-policy is set to
# STRICT`. The sentry is a separate binary under gvisor-bin/, beside runsc.
#
# To bump: change both lines. GVISOR_SHA256 is the sha256 of
# gvisor-x86_64.tar.zstd from that release's SHA256SUMS. Upstream publishes no
# loose runsc binary; the URL the gVisor docs still name returns 404.
# zeroroot-ai/.github version-links.yaml watches google/gvisor releases.
GVISOR_VERSION=release-20260928.0
GVISOR_SHA256=1f2a732d12072eda6b8a64eccf9829fe9f4a1893d3292a7e8005a82089811d8d
